delivery-w4.rktd read delivery-pending; and a rolled-back wave keeps a leading completion-outbox event. A second, independent red was observed and fixed inside this wave: CI check `test (1)` failed on the wave's own PR because adding a test file creates a new ownership family, and the versioned baseline artifacts/tier-ownership/v1.00.29-w0/ownership-matrix.json must be regenerated with it. Rows turn green only when W1-W5 register guards that refuse their injected defect; W6 replays them in expect-refused mode."))) (focused-tests . #hasheq((command . "raco test tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt ; raco test tests/test-milestone-gate.rkt") (detail . "10 tests passed, 0 failures at head 65edf0ec: register is the frozen F1-F10 set; every row carries its contract fields; register matches the raw plan excerpt and the contract document verbatim on all four contract columns, plus observed/evidence-gap verbatim from the excerpt, WITH the converse check (no invented row); exactly one expect-refused fixture per row; the status vocabulary exposes no passing value for an unguarded row; the expect-refused self-test observes guarded-pass and guarded-fail and restores the empty registry via dynamic-wind; W0 registers no guard; SHA256SUMS digests match the content of the files they cover.") (result . "passed"))) (format-compile . #hasheq((command . "raco fmt -i tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt ; raco make tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt") (detail . "raco fmt produced no diff; raco make clean on the one touched Racket module") (result . "passed"))) (lint . #hasheq((command . "racket scripts/check-deps.rkt ; racket scripts/tier-ownership-matrix.rkt check ; racket scripts/metrics.rkt --lint") (detail . "all external packages declared in info.rkt; tier-ownership matrix green (997 rows, the new test registered boundary=integration speed=fast suite=extensions); all 5 static metrics match README.md (test files 1502, test lines 276728, test assertions 41904). The repository 18-check CI lint (format, version-sync, version-validate, version-cross, version-expectations, protocols, imports, deps, metrics-sync, metrics-lint, prose, readme-status, changelog-dates, tests, deprecation, ci-readiness, ivg, doc-freshness) also passed at this head. tests/test-milestone-gate.rkt (75 passed) covers the v1.00.29-w0 ownership-matrix drift gate that this wave had to satisfy after adding a test family.") (result . "passed"))) (fast . #hasheq((command . "racket scripts/run-tests.rkt --suite fast") (detail . "PASS at head 65edf0ec, measured in the worktree whose base-dir resolves to itself (/tmp/q-v10031-w0): files=1202 pass=1202 fail=0 timeout=0 skip=0; tests=17902 pass=17902 fail=0; wall-clock-seconds=1002.635") (result . "passed"))) (remaining-items . (#hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W5 owner (artifact provenance and determinism)") (rationale . "scripts/run-tests/classify-metadata.rkt's resolve-base-dir prefers <parent>/q when the launch directory's parent contains a q/ directory. A wave worktree created as a SIBLING of the canonical checkout therefore makes the entire test runner scan the canonical checkout instead of the worktree, so a wave can verify a DIFFERENT tree and report green. Measured in this wave: two --suite fast runs from /home/user/src/q-agent/wt-v10031-w0 reported 1202 files / 17963 tests while the same suite from /tmp/q-v10031-w0 reported 1202 files / 17902 tests. The plan forbids measuring a different checkout but nothing enforces it; the fix lives under scripts/, outside W0's declared scope, so W5 owns it (checksum/environment provenance is W5's subject).")) #hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "W5 owner (artifact provenance and determinism)") (rationale . "No gate recomputes or validates the versioned baseline artifacts/tier-ownership/v1.00.29-w0/SHA256SUMS, and run-tier-ownership-check ignores it and never validates the matrix's own families/families_digest header fields. The round-4 review found the SIBLING CHECKSUM ALREADY STALE (eb2407c9 vs 2bed7268) and this wave refreshed it by hand per docs/reports/CI-EXIT-TRUTH-v1.00.30.md; a tests/ checksum guard would make that class self-detecting. A fix needs scripts/ or a new tests/ guard, so it lands in W5.")) #hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W6 owner (adversarial permanence rehearsal)") (rationale . "F2-F10 reproduction fixtures read their recorded fields instead of recomputing, because they reference the unmerged W4 branch ce13d038 and live GitHub API responses that do not exist in the tree; only F1 executes live. Documented in the harness and in the contract document's provenance section. W6 exercises these rows for real by replaying each injected defect through the W1-W5 guards.")) #hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "W1 owner (invocation-contract enforcement)") (rationale . "tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt's status-vocabulary comment says the vocabulary 'contains no passing value at all' while the list explicitly includes guarded-pass. The property that matters - an unguarded row can only be reported unguarded - does hold; only the wording is self-contradictory.")) #hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "W2 owner (evidence identity and digest integrity)") (rationale . "Two fidelity gaps in the harness: (a) it does not cross-check each reproduction's owning-wave against its register row (one fixture per row, expect=refused and guard-status vocabulary are enforced; the data agrees by inspection F1->W1 ... F10->W3); (b) the contract-document check compares the four contract columns but not the document's Observed cell or its separate 'Evidence gap per mode' table, which the raw-excerpt check does cover. Both land with W2's other binding guards.")))))
